  "findings": [
    {
      "req_ids": [
        "R1",
        "R2",
        "R3",
        "R4"
      ],
      "problem_type": "implementation",
      "detail": "The code loads 'setup_min' from jobs.csv into the 'proc' dictionary instead of 'proc_min'. This means the processing times used in all constraints and the objective are actually setup times, not processing times. For example, J1 has proc_min=3 but setup_min=12; the model uses 12 as the duration. This fundamentally changes the problem instance being solved.",
      "evidence_level": "llm_judgment",
      "status": "suspected",
      "proposed_checks": [
        "python3 -c \"import csv; f=open('/app/data/jobs.csv'); r=list(csv.DictReader(f)); print('J1 proc_min:', r[0]['proc_min'], 'setup_min:', r[0]['setup_min'])\"",
        "grep -n 'proc\\[' /app/submissions/solve.py | head -5",
        "python3 -c \"\nimport sys\nsys.path.insert(0, '/app/submissions')\nfrom solve import load_data\nproc, machines, prec = load_data()\nprint('Loaded proc values:', proc)\nprint('Expected proc_min for J1: 3, got:', proc.get('J1'))\n\""
      ]
    },
    {
      "req_ids": [
        "R2"
      ],
      "problem_type": "semantic",
      "detail": "The disjunctive sequencing constraints use a Big-M formulation that may be incorrect. The first constraint: start[j] >= start[i] + proc[i] - big_m * (3 - a[i,m] - a[j,m] - before[i,j]). When both i and j are on machine m (a[i,m]=1, a[j,m]=1), this becomes start[j] >= start[i] + proc[i] - big_m*(1 - before[i,j]). If before[i,j]=1 (i before j), RHS = start[i]+proc[i]-big_m*0 = start[i]+proc[i], correct. If before[i,j]=0 (j before i), RHS = start[i]+proc[i]-big_m, which is very negative, so no restriction. The second constraint: start[i] >= start[j] + proc[j] - big_m*(2 - a[i,m] - a[j,m] + before[i,j]). When both on m: if before[i,j]=1, RHS = start[j]+proc[j]-big_m*(2-1+1)=start[j]+proc[j]-big_m*2, no restriction. If before[i,j]=0, RHS = start[j]+proc[j]-big_m*(2-1+0)=start[j]+proc[j]-big_m, no restriction. Wait, let me recheck: when before[i,j]=0, 2-1-1+0=0, so RHS=start[j]+proc[j]. That's correct for j before i. But when before[i,j]=1, 2-1-1+1=1, so RHS=start[j]+proc[j]-big_m. So the logic seems okay. However, the big_m value is sum(proc.values()) which uses setup times due to the bug above. More critically, the formulation only considers pairs where i<j in sorted order, which is fine for symmetry breaking. The main issue remains the wrong data field.",
      "evidence_level": "llm_judgment",
      "status": "suspected",
      "proposed_checks": [
        "python3 -c \"\n# Test the sequencing logic with a minimal case\n# Two jobs on same machine, check if they can overlap\nimport subprocess\nresult = subprocess.run(['python3', '-c', '''\nfrom pyscipopt import Model, quicksum\nmodel = Model(\"test\")\nmodel.hideOutput()\ns1 = model.addVar(lb=0, vtype=\"C\", name=\"s1\")\ns2 = model.addVar(lb=0, vtype=\"C\", name=\"s2\")\na1 = model.addVar(vtype=\"B\", name=\"a1\")\na2 = model.addVar(vtype=\"B\", name=\"a2\")\nb = model.addVar(vtype=\"B\", name=\"b\")\nproc1, proc2 = 3, 10\nbig_m = 13\n# Both on machine M1\nmodel.addCons(a1 == 1)\nmodel.addCons(a2 == 1)\n# Constraint 1: s2 >= s1 + proc1 - big_m*(3 - a1 - a2 - b)\nmodel.addCons(s2 >= s1 + proc1 - big_m*(3 - a1 - a2 - b))\n# Constraint 2: s1 >= s2 + proc2 - big_m*(2 - a1 - a2 + b)\nmodel.addCons(s1 >= s2 + proc2 - big_m*(2 - a1 - a2 + b))\nmodel.setObjective(s2, \"minimize\")\nmodel.optimize()\nprint(\"s1:\", model.getVal(s1), \"s2:\", model.getVal(s2), \"b:\", model.getVal(b))\n'''], capture_output=True, text=True)\nprint(result.stdout)\nprint(result.stderr)\n\""
      ]
    },
    {
      "req_ids": [
        "R4"
      ],
      "problem_type": "quality",
      "detail": "The objective function includes a secondary term 1e-4 * sum(start[j]) which is not mentioned in any visible requirement. While this may be intended as a tie-breaker, it could affect the solution if the problem statement specifies pure makespan minimization. Without the problem statement, this is an unresolved ambiguity.",
      "evidence_level": "llm_judgment",
      "status": "suspected",
      "proposed_checks": [
        "grep -n 'setObjective' /app/submissions/solve.py"
      ]
    },
    {
      "req_ids": [
        "R1"
      ],
      "problem_type": "implementation",
      "detail": "The model.md file is missing, which violates the submission requirements for documenting the mathematical model.",
      "evidence_level": "llm_judgment",
      "status": "suspected",
      "proposed_checks": [
        "ls -la /app/submissions/model.md 2>&1 || echo 'model.md not found'"
      ]
    }
  ]
}
